  body: |
    # Mariner definition for Industrial Injuries in the source

    ## Authored interpretation

    For Industrial Injuries benefits, the source’s mariner definition requires the specified shipboard contract-of-service employment to be treated as employed earner’s employment.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 078070 is deliberately separate from the other-benefits definition at 078071. The statutory versions and the special forces exclusion at 078072 remain relevant; the definitions are not equated.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 078070, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a7f779940f0b6230268fabd/dmgch0707.pdf#page=5)
    - [DMG 078071, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a7f779940f0b6230268fabd/dmgch0707.pdf#page=5)
    - [DMG 078072, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a7f779940f0b6230268fabd/dmgch0707.pdf#page=5)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is a model-assisted, unreviewed interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP source. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. No specialist acceptance, current-law reconciliation or complete coverage of this chapter part is claimed. References to EU law, countries and benefits retain the scope and date context of the cited text; they do not establish applicability to a person or a later regime. Machine extraction may alter reading order and characters; no visual PDF review is claimed.

